<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Partial Info.plist for the TheGoodGuest app target, merged into the
  generated Info.plist at build time (GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE = YES +
  INFOPLIST_FILE — the same merge the Live Activity extension relies on).
  It exists because CFBundleURLTypes is an array-of-dicts no INFOPLIST_KEY_*
  build setting can express.

  The one URL scheme is Google Sign-In's redirect back into the app: the
  REVERSED_CLIENT_ID of the project's iOS OAuth client (a public identifier —
  it ships in every app bundle's Info.plist; the web committed its Firebase
  config on the same reasoning). GoogleSignIn raises at sign-in time if this
  scheme is missing; SignInWithGoogle.preflight checks the registration
  against the live GoogleService-Info.plist first and refuses with a readable
  message instead, and a test pins that the two files agree.

  Kept OUTSIDE the TheGoodGuest/ synchronized folder deliberately: a
  file named into INFOPLIST_FILE that is also swept up as a bundle resource
  is the "multiple commands produce Info.plist" failure the Live Activity
  needed a membership exception to escape.

  ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption lives here rather than in an INFOPLIST_KEY_*
  build setting because that block is duplicated across Debug and Release and
  an export declaration that differed between them would be worse than absent.
  Without it, App Store Connect asks the export-compliance question on EVERY
  TestFlight upload and holds the build until it is answered.

  THE DECLARATION, and what it rests on: this app uses no proprietary or
  non-exempt encryption. Everything cryptographic in it is either a standard
  algorithm used for authentication (CryptoKit's SHA-256, hashing the Sign in
  with Apple nonce — a hash, not a cipher), the platform Keychain, or HTTPS
  provided by the OS. All three fall under the standard exemptions. If that
  ever stops being true — a bundled cipher, a custom protocol, anything
  encrypting user data with keys the app manages — this value has to change
  and the CCATS question becomes real.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption</key>
	<false/>
	<key>CFBundleURLTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>CFBundleTypeRole</key>
			<string>Editor</string>
			<key>CFBundleURLSchemes</key>
			<array>
				<string>com.googleusercontent.apps.502805861152-0p9vjhaf50ecb46j2n8djg7vgrqoale6</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
